From 22f667aef25c0f76ce187d094225506628017845 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:19:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 26/32] vrend: keep the EGL native fence for the GLES hosts
 that need it

Creating an EGL native fence makes the GL driver submit a command
buffer and export a semaphore for every guest fence. A host driver
with no kernel fence of its own emulates the descriptor, and the
per-fence command buffers pile up unrecycled while the guest keeps
fencing: a sample of a desktop GL host taken 30 s into a conformance
run shows 48000 live driver command allocators and 2.2 million driver
resource pools, several gigabytes of host memory, all created under
eglCreateSyncKHR.

The renderer only ever asks a fence whether its work has finished, and
the GL sync object answers that. Use the native fence only on the GLES
hosts whose fence-descriptor path it was written for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 6ec1e87..366e304 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -8007,7 +8007,18 @@ int vrend_renderer_init(const struct vrend_if_cbs *cbs, uint32_t flags)
       vrend_state.use_external_blob = true;
 
 #ifdef HAVE_EPOXY_EGL_H
-   vrend_state.use_egl_fence = virgl_egl_supports_fences(egl);
+   /* An EGL native fence asks the GL driver for a fence it can hand out as a
+    * file descriptor, which forces a real command-buffer submission and an
+    * exportable semaphore for every guest fence. A driver with no kernel
+    * fence of its own emulates that, and the per-fence command buffers it
+    * allocates are never recycled while the guest keeps fencing: a GL
+    * workload costs the host gigabytes within a minute. The GL sync object
+    * answers the only question this renderer asks of a fence -- has the work
+    * finished -- so keep the native fence for the GLES hosts whose fence-fd
+    * path it was written for.
+    */
+   vrend_state.use_egl_fence = virgl_egl_supports_fences(egl) &&
+                               vrend_state.use_gles;
 #endif
 
    if (!vrend_check_no_error(vrend_state.ctx0)) {
